--- !u!114 &825066755
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 825066754}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 44d051fe29de9b640b96519b371839a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TD_Game.WitchHouseQuest
  witches:
  - {fileID: 1659428522}
  - {fileID: 1524726002}
  - {fileID: 1796839534}
  - {fileID: 807917596}
  prisoner: {fileID: 337784578}
  prisonerSprite: {fileID: 923770472}
  chainedSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 66b4fdd1c09183f40b6d9381747acc94, type: 3}
  freedSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d4f7dc12327b76944bc2232489856daf, type: 3}
  chains: {fileID: 946448385}
  paintingSpot: {fileID: 265611081}
  paintingSprite: {fileID: 803508356}
  tornPainting: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4fc42e0425ca58d45811b66bb68df7c0, type: 3}
  wholePainting: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0f52802a593cc824ab08344985a9f3f0, type: 3}
  puzzle: {fileID: 825066756}
  marker: {fileID: 795878392}
  speedBonus: 1.3
  freedSpot: {fileID: 380962120}
  whileGuarded:
  - Stranger... no. Run. They will drink your tonalli as they drank mine.
  - '> Who are you? Why do the witches keep you here?'
  - There is no time! Four of them... four... they never sleep.
  afterWitches:
  - They are gone? You... you beat all four of them!
  - But these chains are not iron. They are a spell, woven into that painting on
    the wall.
  - The witches tore it to pieces and hung it upside down. While the picture is broken,
    so am I.
  - 'Please, warrior: put the painting back together.'
  story:
  - Free... I can feel my legs again. Thank you, warrior of the living.
  - "I am Painal, the runner of the gods. I carried the names of the newly dead down
    the nine levels of Mictl\xE1n, so Mictlantecuhtli would know who was coming."
  - "The four witches were once women of the west, the Cihuateteo. Mictl\xE1n took
    their names; they wanted my feet to run back to the world above."
  - They caught me at the crossroads with a song, painted my capture on amate paper
    and tore it apart. A torn picture is a torn fate.
  - '> The painting showed you running, and four shadows closing in.'
  - 'Yes. And now it shows me free. Take this: the Amulet of Painal, feathers of
    the hummingbird and the jaguar.'
  - "Wear it and the wind will carry you. You will need fast feet where you are going...
    Quetzalc\xF3atl does not wait."
  afterReward:
  - I will rest here a while. When my legs are strong, I will run again.
  - The merchants say there is a narrow stretch of the river where a fast warrior
    can jump across. With my amulet, you could fly over it.
--- !u!114 &825066756
